  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nShowers and storms that fired along a boundary to our \nnorth last night will continue to slide south across the area \nthrough this morning. In its wake, mainly dry conditions expected \nacross the area today, although isold showers/storms will be \npossible across the far south later today as a wave passes by. \n\nFocus then shifts to next week. On Sunday night into Monday, \nexpecting convection mainly across northern zones. An isolated \nsevere storm cant be completely ruled out during this time period, \nbut chances for severe look to really lie more during the daytime \nand evening/night hours on Monday, when a convective complex looks \nto form across the midwest and move southeast towards our area. This \nwill be followed by the potential for additional complexes to affect \nthe area Tuesday, Wednesday, and possibly beyond, before drier \nconditions can finally take hold towards the end of the week and \nover the weekend. Important thing to note is this far out, exact\ndetails including timing and path of any complexes are \nuncertain this far out. But, there is increasing confidence in \nsevere weather episodes across the area this week, with damaging\nwind and flood threats. National centers have already outlooked\nthe area for severe and flooding potential with these \ncomplexes.",
